-- test: check
import Prelude
-- FINDINGS.md, B2: `bad` was rejected ("cannot project p.1 … quantity 0"), `ok` was not.
-- (Minimal: one field is enough.) The difference was where the projection is checked:
-- `refl` checks its argument in the unerased context, while an argument at quantity 0
-- (`lem0 p.a`) is checked in the erased fragment, where a 0-quantity structure may be
-- projected. At the pinned toolchain both check: a term whose type is a proposition is
-- checked erased (the G2 fix), which reaches `refl`'s argument too. The kernel rule
-- itself (`Wiz/Core/Check.lean`, `.refl`) now checks `a` in `Γ⁰` too; its regression is
-- on the Wiz side (Tests/Check.lean, `check: quantities`), since the surface form was
-- already covered by G2 here.
structure P where
  a : Nat
def lem0 (0 n : Nat) : n = n := refl n
def ok {0 p : P} : p.a = p.a := lem0 p.a
def bad {0 p : P} : p.a = p.a := refl p.a
